# AIRA responder console (apps/web) — environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (git-ignored, auto-loaded by Next.js) and fill in
# the values. Never commit a real `.env.local`, and never put secrets in source
# (SECURITY.md §1.6 / §6.3). No Supabase Auth keys belong here: AIRA talks to
# Postgres directly and owns its own authentication (SECURITY.md §4).
#
#   cp apps/web/.env.example apps/web/.env.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL  (REQUIRED)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Least-privilege Postgres connection string for the console. Without it, every
# authenticated API route answers 503 "database_not_configured" and login cannot
# work (src/lib/db.ts).
#
# Local Supabase CLI stack (packages/db) — Postgres 17 on 127.0.0.1:54322, with
# database/user/password all `postgres`:
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres"
#
# Hosted Postgres — use the connection string your provider gives you. Prefer the
# POOLED connection URL for the app runtime, and a least-privilege role (NOT a
# superuser, NOT a Supabase service_role/anon key). Most managed providers require
# TLS, so append sslmode=require:
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://aira_app:<password>@<host>:5432/<db>?sslmode=require"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MEDICAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY  (REQUIRED)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 32-byte AES-256-GCM key for encrypting citizen medical profiles at rest
# (SECURITY.md §8.2). The API dependency container builds this eagerly, so a
# missing/invalid key makes EVERY authenticated API route answer 500 — not just
# the medical ones. Supply it as 64 hex chars or base64. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Keep it out of source and backups-in-the-clear; rotating it makes existing
# encrypted profiles unreadable (they degrade to empty, never crash).
MEDICAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY="<64-hex-or-base64>"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AIRA_PUBLIC_ORIGIN  (OPTIONAL)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The canonical origin used for same-origin checks on state-changing routes
# (src/lib/api/http.ts). Leave unset in local dev — the request origin is used.
# Set it in production to the exact public URL of the console so cross-site POSTs
# are rejected.
# AIRA_PUBLIC_ORIGIN="https://console.aira.example"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTIFICATIONS — Email channel (Gmail SMTP)  (OPTIONAL)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The three-channel notification engine (SECURITY.md §13) sends the Email channel
# through nodemailer. These are read ONLY in
# src/lib/notifications/email-sender.ts — never in source elsewhere, never logged
# (SECURITY.md §13 / §1.6).
#
# When SMTP_HOST, SMTP_USER and SMTP_PASS are ALL present, the Email channel is
# active; if any of the three is missing the Email channel degrades to
# `not_attempted` (R10.7) — the app never errors, it just skips email.
#
#   SMTP_HOST   mail server (e.g. smtp.gmail.com) — no sensible default.
#   SMTP_PORT   optional, defaults to 587 (465 implies implicit TLS).
#   SMTP_USER   authenticating account (a Gmail address); also the default From.
#   SMTP_PASS   the credential. For Gmail this MUST be a 16-char App Password
#               (https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords), NOT your real Google
#               account password — regular passwords are rejected by Gmail SMTP and
#               putting a real account password anywhere is forbidden (SECURITY.md §6.3).
#   SMTP_FROM   optional From address; defaults to SMTP_USER.
# SMTP_HOST="smtp.gmail.com"
# SMTP_PORT="587"
# SMTP_USER="your-account@gmail.com"
# SMTP_PASS="<16-char-gmail-app-password>"
# SMTP_FROM="AIRA <your-account@gmail.com>"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTIFICATIONS — Web Push channel (VAPID)  (OPTIONAL)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Web Push channel (web-push protocol) is read ONLY in
# src/lib/notifications/web-push-sender.ts. When VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY and
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY are both present the channel is active; if either is missing
# the Web Push channel degrades to `not_attempted` (R10.7). Web push also requires
# the service worker at apps/web/public/sw.js (already committed) to receive push
# events in the browser.
#
#   VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY   public key — ALSO exposed to the browser/service worker to
#                      register the push subscription (this is expected: the public
#                      key is not a secret under the Web Push protocol).
#   VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY  private signing key — SERVER ONLY, treat as a secret.
#   VAPID_SUBJECT      a `mailto:` address or an https origin URL identifying the
#                      sender; defaults to mailto:ops@aira.ph when unset.
#
# Generate your OWN keypair with (run from apps/web):
#   npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
#
# >>> DEV-ONLY THROWAWAY KEYS <<<
# The keypair below was generated with the command above purely so local web push
# works out of the box. It is NOT a real secret and MUST NEVER be used in
# production — every deployment MUST generate and set its own VAPID keys and keep
# the private key out of source control.
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY="BBtUTnRETqtKc7MtAC7_Lr_AK005ro70DNoPusAKaYQqdzztbQku5qMpaoq9UuJVz5Fmm29cFDxqgcEOlDaU8Sc"
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY="W0ALZGr6PwEAnqqbKNiODjdc-tLqU7GF4dCdjnncwpo"
# VAPID_SUBJECT="mailto:ops@aira.ph"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NODE_ENV  (set by the tooling — do not hardcode here)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `next dev` runs as development (Secure-cookie flag off so http://localhost works);
# `next build` / `next start` run as production (Secure cookies enforced).
